ead":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.051103535086707036,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.001035400300324103,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":33.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.04306839676252705,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":3.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.035534646216327404,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":7.2,"_gate_margins":0.02065594237375641,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":70.7,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.05018164830604288,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.003737242749523648,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.01954,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":13.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Brookdale Senior Living Inc. owns, manages, and operates senior living communities in the United States. It operates in three segments: Independent Living, Assisted Living and Memory Care, and Continuing Care Retirement Communities (CCRCs). The Independent Living segment owns or leases communities comprising independent and assisted living units in a single community that are primarily designed for middle to upper income seniors. The Assisted Living and Memory Care segment owns or leases communities consisting of freestanding, multi-story communities and freestanding single-story communities, which offer housing and 24-hour assistance with activities of daily living for the Company's residents. This segment operates memory care communities for residents with Alzheimer's and other dementias. The CCRCs segment owns or leases communities that provides various living arrangements, such as independent and assisted living, memory care, and skilled nursing; and services to accommodate various levels of physical ability and healthcare needs. It manages communities on behalf of others. The company was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Brentwood, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Nikolas W. Stengle | CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22K people. Revenue per employee of $142K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $736 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $532 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Brookdale Senior Living Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.2B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $17M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -8.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 10.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (19.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 65/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.11) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 45% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Brookdale (BKD) stock is trading lower today","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/bkd/news/why-up-down/why-brookdale-bkd-stock-is-trading-lower-today","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992842.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Brookdale expects $495M-$502M 2026 adjusted EBITDA as RevPAR growth guidance shifts to 7.4%-7.9% (NYSE:BKD)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668446-brookdale-expects-495m-502m-2026-adjusted-ebitda-as-revpar-growth-guidance-shifts-to-7_4","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992039.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.606,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Brookdale (BKD) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/brookdale-bkd-q3-2026-earnings-184931000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793991518.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Brookdale (NYSE:BKD) misses Q3 2026 sales expectations","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/brookdale-nyse-bkd-misses-q3-113803966.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793965083.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.586,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Brookdale Senior Living Q3 Earnings Call Highlights","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/brookdale-senior-living-q3-earnings-221434336.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003274.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"tit